    "summary": "Domestic flights connecting Puntland and Mogadishu were suspended today after the Somali government imposed a requirement that passengers possess a National Identification Card issued by NIRA. Passengers at Garowe Airport were turned back.",
    "content": "Domestic flights between Puntland and Mogadishu were suspended today following the Somali federal government's implementation of a new requirement that all domestic travelers must present a National Identification Card (NIRA) issued by the National Identification and Registration Authority. The directive took effect this morning, leading to the cancellation of scheduled services.\n\nAt Garowe Airport, passengers booked on Freedom Airlines' Garowe–Mogadishu–Nairobi route were reportedly turned away after it was confirmed that the NIRA card was mandatory for travel. The flights did not proceed as planned, leaving many travelers stranded.\n\nThe NIRA card was introduced as part of a national effort to establish a unified identification system. However, its rollout has been gradual, and many citizens, particularly in regions like Puntland, have not yet obtained the card. The requirement's sudden enforcement has raised concerns about its impact on freedom of movement within the country.\n\nPuntland authorities have previously expressed reservations about federal initiatives that they perceive as infringing on regional autonomy. The suspension of flights highlights the practical challenges of implementing national policies in a federal system where regional administrations often have differing priorities.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development poses significant obstacles. Many diaspora members travel frequently between Puntland and Mogadishu for business, family, and humanitarian purposes. The sudden halt in flights disrupts these connections and could delay essential activities. Additionally, the requirement may complicate travel plans for those who have not yet acquired the NIRA card, as obtaining it from abroad can be cumbersome.\n\nThis incident underscores the ongoing tensions between the federal government and Puntland over the scope of national policies. It also raises questions about the readiness of the NIRA system to handle domestic travel requirements. As of now, there is no clear indication of when flights will resume or whether the requirement will be adjusted to accommodate those without the card.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/01/duulimaadyo-u-dhexeeya-puntland-iyo-muqdisho-oo-maanta-baaqday-kadib-shuruudda-kaarka-aqoonsiga-nira/",
